BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Container Gardening: Supporting Our Local Pollinators in Small Spa
 ces
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T163000
UID:69b1c8968d5e2d093364a64f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators need a supply of nectar throughout the growing sea
 son\, so if you are planting up pots for your garden or balcony\, why not 
 choose plants that will attract birds\, bees\, and butterflies?\nThis demo
 nstration\, led by a Toronto Master Gardener\, will start with how to choo
 se soil\, plants\, and containers\, and how to arrange them to maximize th
 eir positive impact on the environment. At the end of the demonstration\, 
 materials will be shared with participants\, while supplies last.\nThis pr
 ogram is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by 
 Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.\nAll are welcome. No r
 egistration necessary.\nOptional registration is available for those who w
 ish to receive a reminder email or courtesy phone call prior to the event.
  Register online\, or by visiting or calling the branch.
LOCATION:Danforth/Coxwell\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1c8968d5e2d093364a64f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
